// There is exactly one Mailer implementation, and no test double.`,options:["It is speculative generality: with one product and no test double the factory is pure indirection. Construct it directly and add the seam when a second one is real","It is correct as written; every class should be created through a factory","It violates Liskov because create() returns a pointer","It should be a singleton instead of a factory"],answer:[0],explain:"Patterns are tools with a price: extra types, extra files, an extra hop when reading. A factory earns that price when creation varies or must be hidden from callers. With a single implementation and nothing to substitute in tests, you are paying for flexibility nobody uses. The senior move is to name the trigger that would justify it (a second backend, a fake in tests) and wait for it."},{id:"cfm-smell-shallow-clone",kind:"smell",topic:"L3.prototype",level:2,prompt:"Editing a copied slide changes the original. Name the bug.",code:`class Slide : public Node {
